repository-code: 'https://github.com/RS-010806/yamuna'
abstract: >-
  End-to-end geospatial machine-learning pipeline for mapping land cover,
  detecting built-up encroachment and forecasting its areal and spatial growth
  on the active floodplain of the river Yamuna in Delhi. Random Forest, RBF
  support-vector and fully-convolutional CNN classifiers are scored on one
  shared spatial hold-out; change detection and a logistic growth model coupled
  to a driver-based cellular-automata allocation project encroachment to 2035.
  The floodplain boundary is the authors' real digitized active-floodplain
  polygon; the multi-temporal imagery is a controlled benchmark with exact
  ground truth, not observed reflectance.
keywords:
  - remote sensing
  - land-use/land-cover change
  - floodplain encroachment
  - random forest
  - convolutional neural network
  - cellular automata
  - spatio-temporal forecasting
  - Yamuna
